{"id":"fb_1773159308071_l6n07r","signal":"negative","context":"I attempted to push verified work from an isolated worktree to a shared active remote branch. The worktree was isolated, but the branch was not, which violated branch isolation expectations in a multi-agent repo.","whatWentWrong":"I treated filesystem isolation as sufficient and attempted to push to a branch that another agent could also be updating. That risks racing collaborators even when using a separate worktree.","whatToChange":"Always create a unique branch per implementation worktree. Never push to a shared active branch. If the remote branch moves, stop and re-integrate onto a fresh isolated branch before pushing.","whatWorked":"Stopping at the non-fast-forward rejection prevented overwriting the shared branch. Converting the lesson into explicit repo mandates and durable memory is the correct follow-up.","tags":["git","worktree","branch-safety","process","multi-agent"],"skill":"git-worktree-isolation","rubric":{"rubricId":"default-v1","weightedScore":0,"failingCriteria":[],"failingGuardrails":[],"judgeDisagreements":[],"promotionEligible":true},"actionType":"store-mistake","actionReason":null,"timestamp":"2026-03-10T16:15:08.065Z","richContext":{"domain":"git-workflow","filePaths":[],"errorType":null,"outcomeCategory":"standard-failure"}}
